    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a very specific take. But doesn't that basically just legitimize any expansion of power by calling it \"dynamic\"? If we accept that the contract is constantly being \"rewritten\" by the state to meet new threats, aren't we essentially saying the social contract is meaningless because the state can just redefine its obligations whenever it wants? Isn't that just a path to authoritarianism?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
